            "sources": {
                "parts": "Hides stretched over a frame of ash laths and gunwales, about two fifths hide by weight",
                "shell": "Raw cowhide is 2 to 6 mm thick. A blow springs back off the hide unless a lath backs it where it lands: by the model, laths 2.5 cm deep and 0.8 voxel wide every 3 voxels back 27% of the sides, and floor battens 1.4 every 2 back 70% of the bottom. A breaker presses the hide onto the laths, each bending under its share of the side over the 10.3 voxels from the floor to the inwale",
                "depthMetres": "Keel to gunwale amidships: a 5 cm draft with its rower in a 100 kg hull and about 0.4 m of side above it",
                "waterplaneSquareMetres": "A 4 m hull 1.1 m wide, full amidships, so that 1500 L aboard settles her by her 0.4 m of side",
                "seep": "Hide seams and stitch holes weep once the tallow has washed out of them, a little at every seam; Aran crews dressed their currachs every few days"
